      "enacting_law": "not_recorded",
      "effective_date": "not_recorded",
      "verification": "not_recorded",
      "verification_note": "Withholding Tax Facts, January 2024 through December 2024 (https://www.marylandcomptroller.gov/content/dam/mdcomp/tax/legal-publications/facts/Withholding-Tax-Facts-2024.pdf, sha256 4b5b732523daabd51ef6db90f9da47c369c289a3cbc08411c4064ed1c5ad2096, retrieved 2026-11-10) states the 2024 Schedules I and II and a $3,200 personal exemption. It does not state the 2024 standard deduction (15% of AGI, minimum $1,800 single / $3,650 joint, maximum $2,700 single / $5,450 joint) or the exemption phase-out steps. The 2024 Income Tax Summary Report (https://www.marylandcomptroller.gov/content/dam/mdcomp/md/reports/annual/summary24.pdf, sha256 320975967bc1fad247537ff46622e1dbce6401e52a181fa79a876b726cf20425, retrieved 2026-11-10) restates that 2024 rate schedule and does not state those deduction amounts. The 2025 resident booklet restates the 2025 schedules, including 6.25% and 6.50%, the flat standard deduction of $3,350 single / $6,700 joint, and the $3,200 exemption chart. Tax-General section 10-105 as amended by the Budget Reconciliation and Financing Act of 2025 (Chapter 604 / HB 352) matches the 2025 brackets and, for tax years 2025 through 2028, the additional 2% on net capital gain when federal AGI is over $350,000.",
